     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"The target is an OR of h5_0, h5_1 and h5_2, so all three must be cut. Blocking h2_2:obtain removes h3_2:reach, since h2_2 is its only parent. That in turn kills h4_1, h4_2, h5_0 and h5_1. However, h5_2:escalate is still reachable through h3_0:escalate, which comes from h2_1, which needs h1_0 and h1_1, all of which are reachable from the footholds. Blocking h3_0 closes that path. One block is not enough: h5_2 has two independent sources (the h3_2 chain via h2_2 and the h3_0 chain via h2_1, h1_0 and h1_1), and they share no blockable step. So the minimum is 2, for example {h2_2:obtain, h3_0:escalate}.\"}"
    }
